# The release managers: the members of the release managers' team, one GitHub login per line.
# release-approval-check.sh counts an approval of a pull request only from one of them, and only
# when they wrote none of it. The release check job has no secret to read the team with, and the
# repository is public (anyone with a read-only account can leave an approval), so the list is kept
# here, where CODEOWNERS gives it to the release managers: a change to it is reviewed by them.
# Keep it equal to the team. Logins are compared without regard to case. Comments and blank lines
# are ignored; a line that is not a login stops the release.
